## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Low (add assertions) | Eliminates false-pass risk |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Low (split into 2 tests) | Ensures both paths are covered |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Medium (async refactor) | Removes 2s delay + flakiness |
| 4 | **Mystery Guest** | Low (inline data) | Fixes portability & CI failures |
| 5 | **Exception Handling** | Low (one-line refactor) | Cleaner, safer exception testing |
| 6 | **Eager Test** | Medium (decompose or tag) | Better failure isolation |
| 7 | **Magic Number Test** | Medium (derive values) | Self-documenting assertions |
| 8 | **Sensitive Equality** | Low (assert on properties) | Decouples from formatting |
| 9 | **General Fixture** | Trivial (delete field) | Reduces noise |

---

**Bottom line:** 7 of 8 tests exhibit at least one cataloged smell. The highest-priority fixes are the **Assertion-Free Test** (silent false-pass) and **Conditional Test Logic** (hidden coverage gap) — both are quick wins that immediately improve trust in the suite.
